# agent-sandbox environment

## Running commands
{{if .Hook}}- Run shell commands with your normal Bash/Monitor tools; a PreToolUse hook transparently routes each one through the sandbox.
- Command output is returned inline in the tool result.
{{else}}- The Bash and Monitor tools are disabled; use the `run_command` MCP tool to run shell commands.
- Command output is written to files; read the returned stdout/stderr paths.
{{end}}- Allowed commands run directly on the host; all others run through a host-side command broker, each in its own `nono run` sandbox scoped to the working directory.

## Filesystem: the same paths everywhere
There is no container and no bind mount — sandboxed commands run directly on the host filesystem, restricted to the current working directory (read+write):
- Host commands (the allow list below) run in the real project directory using real host absolute paths.
- Sandboxed commands run in that same directory at that same absolute path — no translation needed. HOME keeps its real host value.
- Paths outside the working directory are visible to a sandboxed command only as read-only paths pulled in by non-credential `sandbox.host` capabilities (e.g. `go`, `python`). Raw `sandbox.host.allow/read/allow_file/read_file` grants and the credential capabilities (`docker`, `ssh`) apply to the launched agent only, never to a sandboxed command.
{{if .Safe}}
